        "pkcontributionId": 63492,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uterine ligaments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63493,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are typically an incidental finding.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63494,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About one&nbsp;quarter of thoroughly examined broad ligaments contain adrenocortical remnants {13231045}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63495,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63496,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is uncertain whether these are a result of abnormal detachment of cortical tissue during the embryonic migration of the adrenal glands {23603421} or a result of coelomic epithelial metaplasia {6108244}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63497,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are usually grossly occult, but if visible, they are a few millimetres in size and appear yellow.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63498,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The remnants form round nests or cords of pale lipid-rich cells resembling the cortex of the adrenal gland. They are usually single, although sometimes multiple. Hyperplasia and adenoma are rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63499,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63500,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 216,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:46:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
